## v0.6.5 – Persist ActionBar Settings to Database

**Date:** December 19, 2025

### Changes Made:
- Added `actionbar` column (PostgreSQL text array) to User model for storing enabled button IDs
- Initialize `actionbar` to empty array on user signup instead of null
- Updated auth handler responses (login, signup, profile) to include `actionbar` field
- Added `PATCH /auth/profile` endpoint for updating user profile settings
- Added `updateProfile` function to frontend authApi service
- Added `updateActionbar` method to AuthContext for saving preferences
- Refactored ActionBar component to load settings from user data with localStorage fallback
- ActionBar now properly resets when switching between user accounts
- Fixed bug where localStorage from previous user would bleed into new user session
- ActionBar defaults all toggle buttons (Pomodoro, Break, Meeting) to hidden/off
- Added comprehensive backend tests for actionbar functionality (6 tests)
- Added frontend tests for ActionBar component behavior (10 tests)

### Current Status:
- ActionBar settings now persist to database and sync across devices
- New users get empty actionbar array (all toggle buttons hidden by default)
- Existing users' preferences load from database on login
- localStorage serves as cache for offline/fast hydration
- All backend and frontend tests passing

### Unresolved Issues:
- None

